Exp :Replacing of string

Aim:
To write a Java program to replace a word or character in a given string using the replace() method.

Algorithm:
1. Start the program.
2. Import the Scanner package.
3. Read a string from the user.
4. Read the old word and the new word.
5. Use the replace() method to replace the old word with the new word.
6. Display the replaced string.
7. Stop the program.

Program:

import java.util.Scanner;
public class ReplaceString {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        String str, oldWord, newWord;

        System.out.print("Enter a string: ");
        str = sc.nextLine();

        System.out.print("Enter the word to replace: ");
        oldWord = sc.nextLine();

        System.out.print("Enter the new word: ");
        newWord = sc.nextLine();

        String result = str.replace(oldWord, newWord);

        System.out.println("Replaced string = " + result);

        sc.close();
    }
}

